WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.801
-Bobby Moynihan right here,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:04.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
I want to talk about this.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:06.000
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.300
-Did you get to talk to Margot?
I know Margot hosted the show

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.701
"SNL," when you were
a cast member.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:11.868
-Yeah, she was wonderful
when she came.

00:00:11.868 --> 00:00:13.667
I had written a sketch called
"The Librarian"

00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.067
that I tried to get on like
many, many times.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.467
And she came and she knocked it
out of the park.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:20.167
And she nailed it.
Yeah.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.234
-What do you remember about
"Saturday Night Live"?

00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:23.968
Were you nervous when you first
got on the show?

00:00:23.968 --> 00:00:25.300
-No, I was fine.

00:00:25.300 --> 00:00:28.234
[ Laughter ]
-Wow! No story here.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.701
You were telling me backstage,
was it the week before

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.734
or the night before,
you just got on

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.467
"Saturday Night Live."
Wasn't announced.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:38.033
-Yeah, yeah, the night before
my first Monday.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:40.400
So it was the Sunday night
before I'm supposed to go in.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.834
My life's dream
has now come true.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.167
I couldn't believe it.

00:00:44.167 --> 00:00:46.434
And I went to
Upright Citizens Brigade,

00:00:46.434 --> 00:00:48.601
which they had
a show there called Asssscat,

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:50.934
and we would perform there.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:52.868
And I went, and I was like,
"Oh, my gosh!"

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.434
Like, "I'm gonna start 'SNL'
tomorrow.

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:56.801
This is amazing."
And I was in my own head.

00:00:56.801 --> 00:00:59.334
And five minutes
before the show started,

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:01.067
Robin Williams walks in.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.300
And he's just --
they're just like,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.567
"Hey, do you mind if Robin
performs with you?"

00:01:03.567 --> 00:01:05.367
And I was like, "What?!"

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:08.300
And Robin Williams showed up
and did a show with us.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.000
And it was, like,
the second-best thing

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.567
in the world
that could have happened.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.901
-Yeah, "Saturday Night Live."

00:01:14.901 --> 00:01:16.534
You're like, "Wait.
What is going on with my life?"

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.033
-Exactly.
And then, after the show,

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.601
Robin grabbed me
by the shoulders and was like,

00:01:21.601 --> 00:01:24.868
"I have an idea.
Give me your clothes.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.400
I'm gonna go into work
for you tomorrow.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.701
You just got
'Saturday Night Live.'

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.234
Wouldn't it be hilarious
if I went into work for you."

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.300
And I remember
instantly thinking,

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.834
"Oh, no.
This is a terrible idea."

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:38.467
[ Laughter ]
I do not want my first day

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:42.033
at "SNL" to have Lorne Michaels
see Robin Williams walk in

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:44.467
in a Bart Simpson T-shirt.
I was like, "No, this is --"

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:47.367
Don't do bits the first day
at work.

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:50.200
-And I'm like, "How do you
tell Robin Williams no?

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:52.734
And he was 100% serious.

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.634
And then, I was terrified.
He gave me his number.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.667
And I was like, "Oh, no.
This is gonna happen."

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.868
And he never called,
and I was really happy.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.467
-Yeah, he probably thought
about you, said, "Oh, I'm gonna

00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:04.801
let the kid
become a star first."

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.334
-Yeah, I think he thought
it was a fun idea,

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:09.067
and maybe he saw the complete
and total panic in my face.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.267
-Yeah. I want to talk about
this, by the way.

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.367
Look at this.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.467
"Not All Sheep are Boring!"

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:17.634
Congratulations, buddy.
You wrote this book.

00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:20.033
What inspired you to write this?

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.400
-I have a daughter,
5-year-old daughter,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.667
and a lot of bedtime reading

00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:26.400
and started talking about
counting sheep.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.067
And I was like,
"Why do people do that?

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.734
Why do we count sheep,
specifically, to fall asleep?

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:31.868
Are they all boring?"

00:02:31.868 --> 00:02:33.100
And I wanted to get
to the bottom of it.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:34.367
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.968
Wow.
You really solved the case.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.367
-Yeah, I tried to.

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.000
Turns out they're boring,
a little boring sometimes.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.200
-Yeah.
There's a lot of --

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.968
What do you call it?
-Dedication. Yeah.

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:47.033
If a publisher gives you
the chance

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:49.167
to have a thank-you section
in a book,

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.000
you use it
to its full potential.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.501
So, as you can see --
-Yeah, you thanked

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:54.334
a lot of people here.
-Yeah, many.

00:02:54.334 --> 00:02:57.000
And then there's also a website
at the bottom that continues

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.167
people who I forgot to thank
in the sheep dedication.

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:02.901
So you can go to that website.
There's a lot more on there.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:03.934
[ Laughs]

00:03:03.934 --> 00:03:05.501
-I mean, you thank --

00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:07.934
-I thank everybody
from my high school buddies,

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.934
my high school teachers.
-Keanu Reeves?

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:11.634
What has he done for you?

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:12.968
-For me personally?
-For this book.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.868
-I mean, entertained me
my entire life.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:16.167
For this book?
Nothing.

00:03:16.167 --> 00:03:17.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.501 --> 00:03:19.434
-He has nothing to do
with this book, Keanu Reeves?

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:22.000
-Keanu Reeves probably
doesn't know this book exists,

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.133
and I'm fine with that
because he's a nice man

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.334
who treats people well,
and I say, "Thank you, Keanu."

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.734
-Oh, there you go.
I love that.

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:29.467
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:31.634
-He's a really good guy.

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:33.968
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.133
-You thank George Lucas.
Do you know him?

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.434
-Not personally, no.
-There you go, okay.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:38.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.667
The beverage peach Snapple.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:42.200
-Yes, thank you very much.
I love it.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.467
It's a very delicious drink.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:44.834
-I love you put
"the beverage peach."

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.100
Is there another peach Snapple?

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.801
-Oh, just in case you thought
it was the person.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:51.601
-You thanked the beverage.

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:55.067
-Mr. Peach Snapple.
-Mr. Peach Snapple, yeah.

00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.501
And so if you go to
peoplewhodidnotfit

00:03:58.501 --> 00:04:02.334
inthededication
ofnotallsheepareboring...

00:04:02.334 --> 00:04:04.100
-No, it's very easy to read,
Jimmy.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:05.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.400
-That's a great --
how'd you get that website?

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:08.701
It wasn't taken?
-It wasn't taken!

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:10.734
Can you believe it?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.534
-Usually an author, you know,

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:15.367
you'll have the photo
of the author,

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:16.667
you know, in the book.

00:04:16.667 --> 00:04:20.701
The photo you chose is this.
-Yes.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:22.234
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:25.133
-That is --
-That is the boy I hired

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:26.968
to write the book.
-No, no, no.

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.534
[ Laughter ]
He's very talented.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.767
-Yes.
-He wrote this for you.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.501
-Yeah, he's very good.
He's 5.

00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:34.868
He's an author now.
-His name is Peach Snapple.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:36.467
-Peach Snapple.

00:04:36.467 --> 00:04:38.534
-Pete Schnapple.

00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:40.434
Yeah, I can see the confusion.
-Yes.

00:04:40.434 --> 00:04:43.100
-But it looks
like you as a child.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.400
-I mean, nothing has changed.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.667
-You look the same, buddy.
Come on.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:47.968
Well, this guy --

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:51.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.434
Stop making that face.

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:58.767
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:01.300
This boy would be
very proud of this man.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:03.167
He really would.
Congratulations, Bobby Moynihan.

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:04.434
Thank you for
coming on the show.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:05.801
-Thank you so much, man.
It's such a pleasure, as always.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:09.133
-"Not All Sheep are Boring!"
is out tomorrow.

